I've written the plan for this session: two task files and the issue responses are in session_plan/. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the files are on disk but not in git. The harness's || true expects that.

Task 1 (product, Fixes #1074): I filed #1074 during planning from the assessment's first bug. In a fresh git init directory, yoyo doctor ends with "3 issues found. Try /fix", but the three are setup warnings (no config file, no context file, no .yoyo/ memory directory) that /fix can't repair. The footer also tells people using yoyo doctor from the shell to run /fix and /health, which only exist inside yoyo. The task:
• builds the footer from the failing rows and from where it was run (shell or inside yoyo);
• names /fix only when a failing row is a check /fix actually re-runs;
• tests every case against the full expected string, keeps the all-pass output unchanged, and requires the deliberate break-and-restore check (put the old wording back, see the test fail, restore it).

Task 2 (product, Part of #1012): this works through the oldest open self-filed issue. It corrects the prices /cost uses for mistral-large-latest, gemini-2.5-flash and gemini-2.5-flash-lite, which differ from models.dev's. I took them from the 14:40 comment on #1012 and checked that nothing has changed them since.
• src/format/cost.rs is already 8 lines over its size limit (3613 against 3605), so the task must not make it longer. It moves out the two old tests that check the outdated prices, with corrected values, which frees more lines than the new flash-lite price entry adds.
• After the change it compares the full list of rows that still disagree with models.dev before and after, to make sure no other model's price starts disagreeing.

